.hypothesis/

# Local-only multi-GB artifacts (never commit — re-downloadable / re-generable).
# Surgical patterns: DO NOT exclude models/constraint-verifier-v2/ (small,
# intentionally tracked) or output/** files that the conductor already
# committed.  Target only the large re-downloadable / re-generable files.
models/**/*.gguf
models/**/*.mxfp4
models/**/*.safetensors
models/**/*.onnx
models/**/*.onnx_data*
models/gpt-oss-safeguard-20b/
models/gpt-oss-safeguard-120b/
models/openai_privacy_filter/
# ^ Added 2026-04-23 after the conductor's auto-checkpoint committed
#   17 GB of HuggingFace-downloaded model weights (model.safetensors,
#   onnx/*.onnx_data*, original/) into this path.  GitHub's 100 MB
#   per-file limit rejected the push; history was rewritten with
#   git-filter-repo to purge models/openai_privacy_filter/** and the
#   Vivado-generated BD netlists.  These patterns prevent the conductor
#   from re-committing any HuggingFace model tree.  If a model directory
#   must be tracked (e.g. a small hand-built artifact), add a negation
#   with `!models/<dirname>/`.

# Large training checkpoints.  The conductor's bounded-training drivers
# (Thesis-A EBT, etc.) save *.pt checkpoints under results/; one of them
# (results/experiment_3734_checkpoint.pt, 765 MB) exceeded GitHub's 100 MB
# limit and silently blocked every push for 143 commits.  History was
# purged with git-filter-repo 2026-06-03.  These patterns keep checkpoints
# untracked so it cannot recur.  Result JSON artifacts are still tracked.
results/**/*.pt
results/*.pt

# Vivado intermediate / future-build artifacts.  The .gen/ subtree
# contains >100 MB synthesized netlists (carnot_ising_bd_*_sim_netlist.v
# and .vhdl) that GitHub also rejected.
output/carnot_ising_bd/project/carnot_ising.runs/impl_*/
output/carnot_ising_bd/project/carnot_ising.runs/synth_*/
output/carnot_ising_bd/project/.Xil/
output/carnot_ising_bd/project/carnot_ising.gen/
output/carnot_ising_bd/vivado_*.backup.*
output/carnot_ising_bd/*.jou
output/carnot_ising_bd/.Xil/
# Catch-all for Vivado sim netlists regardless of where they land.
output/**/*sim_netlist*.v
output/**/*sim_netlist*.vhdl
output/**/*sim_netlist*.vhd

# Vivado output scratch (2026-05-21 cleanup) — `.jou` (TCL command
# journal) and `.log` (run log) are written to the CWD on every
# Vivado invocation; `vivado_<PID>.backup.{jou,log}` are previous-run
# rotations. None are inputs to anything; future runs regenerate
# fresh ones. Same for webtalk and .Xil scratch dirs. Globally
# ignored so the pattern doesn't recur in any directory.
vivado.jou
vivado.log
vivado_*.backup.jou
vivado_*.backup.log
vivado_*.jou
vivado_*.log
webtalk.jou
webtalk.log
hs_err_pid*.log
**/.Xil/
# Other Vivado run-time scratch (added 2026-05-21 after clockInfo.txt
# appeared at root during an FPGA task). Vivado / Xilinx tools dump
# these to CWD on every invocation; none are project sources.
clockInfo.txt
planAhead.jou
planAhead.log
usage_statistics_webtalk.html
usage_statistics_webtalk.xml
fsm_encoding_report.html
xilinx_dl.log
xsim.dir/
xsim_*.jou
xsim_*.log

# Vivado v4 KV260 build artifacts (Exp 971+) — match the existing
# carnot_ising_bd patterns above. v4 introduced a new project name
# variant.
output/carnot_ising_v4_bd/
output/carnot_ising_v[0-9]*_bd/

# Conductor supervisor test must stay quarantined — running it kills the conductor
tests/python/test_conductor_supervisor.py

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Root-clutter guard (2026-06-09). Agents/experiments repeatedly write one-off
# scratch scripts (probe*.py, check_*.py, test_*.py, append_*.py, fix_*.py, ...)
# into the REPO ROOT instead of scripts/experiments/ or tests/python/. Ignoring
# root-level *.py stops `git add -A` (including the conductor's --no-verify
# commits, which still honor .gitignore) from re-tracking them. Real Python lives
# in python/, scripts/, tests/ — never the repo root. ~155 prior scratch files
# were archived to legacy/root-scratch-2026-06/ in this cleanup. conftest.py and
# setup.py are whitelisted in case a build ever legitimately needs them at root.
/*.py
!/conftest.py
!/setup.py

# LaTeX build artifacts written to the repo root by paper compiles (regenerable)
/main.aux
/main.log
/main.out
/main.bbl
/main.blg
/main.toc
/main.fls
/main.fdb_latexmk
/main.synctex.gz
# Vivado per-invocation clock report written to CWD (regenerable scratch)
/clockInfo.txt
# Quarantine dir for the root-clutter sweeper (scripts/root_clutter_sweep.py) — it
# relocates untracked root scratch here (reversible) instead of hard-deleting it.
.root-scratch-trash/

# Conductor pre-test fingerprint cache — local-only, regenerated on first run
ops/.pretest-cache.json

# QA-layer authenticity audit rotation state — local-only, tracks which
# adversarial_verify.py function-chunk the next milestone-close audit
# starts from, regenerated on first run
ops/.qa_layer_audit_rotation.json

# Vendored EBT repo (has its own .git) — must NOT be committed as a submodule gitlink;
# an orphaned ebt_tmp gitlink with no .gitmodules broke every GitHub Pages build (checkout step).
ebt_tmp/

# Embedded experiment clones (have their own .git) — must NEVER be committed as
# submodule gitlinks. A conductor `git add -A` committed `nano-trm` as a mode
# 160000 gitlink with no .gitmodules (commit c4c612662, 2026-06-06), which broke
# EVERY GitHub Actions checkout (Pages, CI, phase1-reproducer) at
# `fatal: No url found for submodule path 'nano-trm'`. Ignore the embedded repos
# so this cannot recur.
/nano-trm/
/ebt_tmp/
/trm_src/
/hrm_ckpt/
/external/ARC-GEN/
# ARC-AGI-3 Milestone 1 winner repos, cloned for study (2026-07-11) -- each
# has its own .git, same gitlink risk as ARC-GEN above.
/external/duck-harness/
/external/arc-m1-2nd-reki/
/external/arc-m1-3rd-forge/

# Verifier/model weights under results/ -> HuggingFace + IPFS, NOT git (rule 3).
# results/**/*.pt was added 2026-04-23 but missed top-level + .safetensors/.bin/.gguf
# in results/ (25 small verifier safetensors, ~18MB, slipped in). These patterns stop
# NEW verifier/abstraction weights from landing in git as they grow; the binaries live
# on HF/IPFS keyed by CID, referenced from ops/verifier_registry.yaml. (2026-06-08)
results/*.pt
results/*.safetensors
results/*.bin
results/*.gguf
results/*.ckpt

# ARC-AGI-3 SDK local cache (downloaded game envs + recordings) — not source
environment_files/
recordings/
data/arc_public_demo_human_replay_corpus/

# Pytest tmp_path basetemp — ephemeral test outputs, never commit (2026-06-16 security audit)
.tmp-pytest/
recordings/arc_live_submit/
recordings/arc_live_probe/

# Large binary model checkpoints never belong in git (2026-06-20 operator directive). All *.ckpt are
# the retired nano-TRM Sudoku run (~1.4GB, val-0.63, DO_NOT_RELAUNCH, grafted=chance). Use `git add -f`
# to deliberately track a specific small checkpoint if ever needed. (Legitimate SMALL models in models/
# *.safetensors / *.pt stay tracked -- not ignored here.)
*.ckpt

# Generated transition-capture corpus (large npz; regenerated from probes + human replays)
data/arc_transition_corpus/
